{
    "background_story": "Chaim was a Tobagonian steel drummer who brought the vibrant rhythms of his island home to the world. Born and raised in Scarborough, Tobago, he was mesmerized by the sound of the steel drums from a young age. Chaim spent years perfecting his craft, playing on the streets and at local festivals. His big break came when he was invited to perform at the annual Tobago Jazz Experience. Chaim's energetic stage presence and infectious beats quickly won over the crowd, earning him a spot on the international music circuit. As he traveled the world, Chaim remained deeply rooted in his Tobagonian heritage, sharing the rich cultural traditions of his island with every performance. His music became a testament to the beauty and resilience of the Tobagonian spirit.",
